FILE items/thm-compact-iff-fip.md
41:## Statement
42:
43:Let $(X, \mathcal{T})$ be a topological space ([[def-topological-space]]). For a
44:family $\mathcal{A}$ of subsets of $X$ write
45:
46:$$\bigcap \mathcal{A} \;:=\; \{\, x \in X : x \in A \text{ for every } A \in \mathcal{A} \,\},$$
47:
48:so that $\bigcap \varnothing = X$, matching the convention for the empty finite
49:intersection in [[def-finite-intersection-property]]. Then:
50:
51:1. $(X, \mathcal{T})$ is compact ([[def-compact-space]]) **if and only if** every
52:   family $\mathcal{A}$ of closed subsets of $X$ with the finite intersection
53:   property ([[def-finite-intersection-property]]) satisfies
54:   $\bigcap \mathcal{A} \ne \varnothing$.
55:2. Equivalently: $(X, \mathcal{T})$ is compact if and only if every family of
56:   closed subsets of $X$ that is contained in some filter on $X$
57:   ([[def-filter]]) has nonempty intersection, a family of subsets of $X$ lying
58:   in a filter exactly when it has the finite intersection property
59:   ([[lem-fip-generates-filter]]).
60:
61:No choice principle is used in either direction: complementation is a canonical
62:bijection, so no member of a family ever has to be selected.
